  &lt;div class=&quot;note-comment-text&quot;&gt;There is a &amp;quot;yellow +&amp;quot; sign to Mátraháza, a &amp;quot;yellow -&amp;quot; sign to Mátraháza on another route and &amp;quot;yellow -&amp;quot; sign to Kékestető. Together with the &amp;quot;yellow -&amp;quot; sign there is a &amp;quot;blue ^^&amp;quot; called &amp;quot;A Mátra bércein&amp;quot;. This last one is marked as red on the map incorrectly. / Resolved &lt;time title=&quot;25 August 2025 at 21:26&quot; datetime=&quot;2025-08-25T21:26:25Z&quot;&gt;about 9 hours ago&lt;/time&gt; by &lt;a class=&quot;mw-100 d-inline-block align-bottom text-truncate text-wrap&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot; href=&quot;https://www.openstreetmap.org/user/sfphoton&quot;&gt;sfphoton&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class=&quot;note-comment-text&quot;&gt;I checked the relation &amp;quot;A Mátra bércein&amp;quot;, however it does not specify anything red, maybe it&amp;#39;s a default on your renderer: https://www.openstreetmap.org/relation/5563755

I have added colour=blue in an attempt to specify this. Sadly, I could not add the machine-parseable osmc:symbol tag as it is too complex.

I&amp;#39;m closing this note as I think there is nothing else left to do. If you still find this way red, please file an issue for your map application or reopen this note.</title>
